      "role": "user",
      "content": "it wasnt just a delay tho, it felt like his facial muscles didn't quite sync up with the rest of his expressions. it was super uncanny valley. and if you look at his recent stuff compared to like, 5 years ago, the whole vibe is just... different. almost like the way a deepfake or a high-end digital double would struggle with micro-expressions. do u think it's possible that someone's using AI/synthetic tech to manage celebrity public appearances now? like to keep the 'brand' going even if the real person is gone?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
